jobs.description:
Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!

In the role of Quality Control Specialist, you will take charge of preserving product quality at every step of the production cycle. Your key responsibilities involve:
- Carrying out precise measurements and sampling in line with predefined standards;
- Reviewing and authorizing product batches prior to their transfer to storage;
- Overseeing and ensuring quality consistency throughout different production phases;
- Conducting quality assessments based on the established quality plan;
- Ensuring defective products do not proceed into the supply chain.

 - Work full-time in a rotating 5-shift pattern (06:00-14:00, 14:00-22:00, 22:00-06:00);
- Earn a competitive salary of €3,236 monthly, which includes a 28.5% shift bonus;
- Receive a travel reimbursement of €0.23 per kilometer, with no upper limit;
- Access various opportunities to grow personally and professionally within the organization;
- Start saving for your pension from day one under Covebo;
- Enjoy 25 vacation days provided through Covebo;
- Benefit from an 8.33% holiday bonus via Covebo;
- Explore the chance to secure a permanent role with Canpack after your time with Covebo.

 - Excellent command of English, both verbal and written;
- Hands-on experience with tools and methods for quality assurance;
- Exceptional analytical abilities and attention to detail;
- Familiarity with safety protocols and hygiene standards;
- Skilled in using Microsoft Office programs.

 For over 30 years, Canpack Helmond has been a leader in the metal packaging industry. With a strong presence in Central and Eastern Europe and expanding into Western Europe, Asia, and Africa, they are one of the largest manufacturers of metal packaging worldwide. Their dedicated team of nearly 8,000 employees produces approximately 25 billion beverage cans, 28 billion bottle closures, 1 billion metal containers for the food and chemical industries, and 700 tons of glass packaging annually.
